translation.mcpMarketplace.pluginLinkedTitle	Managed by a plugin
translation.mcpMarketplace.pluginLinkedBody	A plugin uses this MCP server and owns its connection settings, which cannot be edited here; the remaining settings are yours to change, and you can still disable it or remove the installation.
translation.mcpMarketplace.pluginLinkedBodyNamed_one	The {{plugins}} plugin uses this MCP server and owns its connection settings, which cannot be edited here; the remaining settings are yours to change, and you can still disable it or remove the installation.
translation.mcpMarketplace.pluginLinkedBodyNamed_other	The {{plugins}} plugins use this MCP server and own its connection settings, which cannot be edited here; the remaining settings are yours to change, and you can still disable it or remove the installation.
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthSetupRequiredTitle	OAuth setup required
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthSetupRequiredBody	This provider cannot create an OAuth client automatically. For API-key authentication, select Authorization header. Use “Bearer ${MCP_API_KEY}” as the value. Then add a write-only secret named “MCP_API_KEY” in the Secrets section. Alternatively, add a pre-registered OAuth client ID under Advanced.
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthCapabilityCheckingTitle	Checking OAuth setup
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthCapabilityCheckingBody	Devin is checking whether this provider can start OAuth safely.
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthCapabilityCheckFailedTitle	OAuth setup check failed
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthCapabilityCheckFailedBody	Devin could not check this provider. Retry before connecting.
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthCapabilityUnknownTitle	OAuth setup could not be verified
translation.mcpMarketplace.oauthCapabilityUnknownBody	Devin could not verify automatic OAuth setup. Check the provider documentation. If the provider uses an API key, select Authorization header. Use “Bearer ${MCP_API_KEY}” as the value. Then add a write-only secret named “MCP_API_KEY” in the Secrets section. Alternatively, add a pre-registered OAuth client ID under Advanced.
